[FEN "r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/2NP4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 0 4"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/2B1P3/2NP4/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR_b_KQkq_-_0_4"]
[Role "exercise"]

{ Your bishop is the piece he fears, so he sends a knight to the rim to hunt it. }
4... Na5 { There it goes, sideways, after your bishop. Do you save it or ignore it? } 5. Nge2 { Just develop. If he takes, your pawn takes back towards the middle. [%csl Ge2] } (5. Bb3 { Saving the bishop. It is fine, but he chases it again later. } 5... Bb4 6. Ne2 d5 { He hits the middle and your bishop has done nothing yet. }) (5. a3 { A useful little move, and also perfectly playable. } 5... Nxc4 6. dxc4 d6 { The same trade, a move later. Level and pleasant. }) (5. Qf3 { The queen guards the bishop. Also good, if a bit early. } 5... c6 6. Nge2 b5 { His pawns come at you and the queen must move again. }) 5... Nxc4 { He trades his rim knight for your good bishop. } 6. dxc4 { Towards the centre. The doubled pawns grip d5 and your play is simple. [%csl Gc4][%cal Gc4d5] } (6. f4 { The Vienna move, at exactly the wrong moment: you are a piece down. } 6... Nb6 7. fxe5 Nh5 { He simply keeps the bishop and you are losing. [%csl Rb6] }) 6... Bc5 { His bishop settles. Now bring the queen to a square that does three jobs. } 7. Qd3 { She watches d5, guards e4 and makes room to castle long. [%csl Gd3] } (7. O-O { Castling is safe and sound, and slightly quieter. } 7... d6 8. Qd3 Be6 { The same idea one move later. Nothing wrong at all. }) (7. h3 { A waiting move when you had a strong square for the queen. } 7... d6 8. Qd3 Be6 { You got there anyway, a move behind. }) (7. f4 { The pawn push, but his knight gets a lovely square. } 7... Ng4 8. h3 Nf2 { The knight dives at your queen and rook again. [%cal Rf2d1] }) 7... d6 { He holds the middle. Offer a trade of his best piece. } 8. Be3 { The bishop offers itself. Either answer leaves you comfortable. [%cal Ge3c5] } (8. O-O { Castling, calm and good. Just a shade less to the point. } 8... Be6 9. Ng3 O-O { Level and pleasant. The trade offer asks a harder question. }) (8. Ng3 { The knight heads for f5. Also fine, if slower. } 8... Be6 9. O-O O-O { Equal. His bishop keeps its good diagonal. }) (8. Na4 { Chasing the bishop with the wrong piece. } 8... Nd7 9. Be3 Bxe3 { You ended up trading anyway, and lost time. }) 1-0


[Event "Vienna: the copycat bishop"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
