[Role "exercise"]

{ Against the Vienna, when he does not fight for the middle, take all of it and say thank you. }
2... d6 { A timid little move that guards a pawn and nothing else. Take your chance. } 3. d4 { Straight ahead. He must give up the middle or defend it a pawn short. [%csl Gd4] } (3. f4 { The gambit, but his pawn on d6 is already propping e5. } 3... exf4 4. Qf3 Nc6 { He takes and you have given away the big centre. }) (3. Nf3 { Solid development. Fine, but the whole middle was on offer. } 3... c5 4. Bc4 Be7 { A normal game. You turned down the free space. }) (3. Bc4 { The bishop first. Also playable, just less to the point. } 3... Be7 4. Nf3 c5 { Equal-ish. The pawn to d4 asks a much harder question. }) (3. Nge2 { A quiet knight route while the centre was begging. } 3... Nf6 4. d4 c6 { You got there anyway, one move behind. }) (3. g3 { The fianchetto. Solid, but you turn down the whole centre. } 3... Nf6 4. Bg2 g6 { He gets his pieces out for free and the moment has passed. }) 3... Be7 { He tucks the bishop in. Keep building. } 4. Nf3 { The knight props d4 and eyes the middle. Everything flows. [%csl Gf3] } (4. dxe5 { Trading in the middle. It only helps him breathe. } 4... dxe5 5. Qxd8+ Bxd8 { Queens off and the position dries up. Nothing gained. }) (4. Be3 { Also good, guarding d4 with a piece. } 4... Nf6 5. h3 c6 { Just as pleasant. Either move keeps your grip. }) (4. d5 { Locking the centre when you had the freer game. } 4... Nd7 5. a4 Ngf6 { The position closes and his cramped pieces get squares. }) 4... Nd7 { His pieces are tripping over each other. Bring the bishop out. } 5. Bc4 { Every piece on a good square while he defends half a board. [%csl Gc4,Gd4] } (5. Be3 { Also fine, and just as good by the numbers. } 5... Ngf6 6. h3 c6 { Equally comfortable. Both bishops have a job. }) (5. h3 { A useful little move, if a slow one. } 5... c6 6. g4 h6 { Also playable, and rather more committal. }) (5. a4 { Space on the wing when the middle is the story. } 5... Ngf6 6. Bc4 O-O { You got the bishop out anyway, a move later. }) 1-0


[Event "Vienna: the fake pin"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/yXmLc1zx/J7TfBHsO"]
[FEN "rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/2N5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 1 2"]
[SetUp "1"]
